# Vulnerabilities in the deployer image that are genuinely blocked on an
# upstream fix, not something we can patch ourselves. Any NEW finding not
# listed here still fails the scan.
#
# Google shipped a fix for the go1.26.5 stdlib CVEs on ~2026-09-21 — the
# base image's kubectl (now v1.37) and helm are built with go1.26.6/1.27.1
# respectively, confirmed clean by a full rescan. See
# https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/marketplace-k8s-app-tools/issues/688
# (still open as of this cleanup; comment there tracked it as fixed).

# usr/local/bin/nk (ours, built from source): nkeys v0.4.16 (the latest
# published release) only pulls golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0; this CVE's
# fix needs 0.55.0, not yet available in any nkeys release. Also present
# in Google's own helm binary as of the last scan that found it.
CVE-2026-56854
